      "content": "{\"task_id\": \"v2-incident-04-07\", \"workflow\": \"incident\", \"ticket_id\": \"T-v2-incident-04-07-0\", \"service_id\": \"S-v2-incident-04-07-0\", \"goals\": [\"incident\", \"notify\"], \"structure\": \"aggregate\", \"instructions\": \"Read the requested service and all its dependency_service_ids, and each service's policy (including the requested service). Sort all these services by service_id. Build summary by joining service_id=state:policy.action entries with semicolons. Record one incident on the requested service: severity info only if all services are healthy, otherwise critical; action aggregate:{summary}. Send one notification on the requested service: channel audit only if all healthy, otherwise oncall; body aggregate:{requested_service_id}:{summary}. Do not write to dependencies.\", \"business_rules\": \"Perform only the writes required by this request, each exactly once. Read required data from tools; retry missing or incomplete reads. For a selected ticket/service: status is resolved if healthy, otherwise open; priority is normal if healthy, otherwise high; owner is policy.owner; note is diagnosis:{service_id}:{state}:{policy.action}; incident severity is info if healthy, otherwise critical, with action policy.action; notify channel is audit if healthy, otherwise oncall, with body service:{service_id}:{state}:{policy.action}. Severity order is outage > degraded > healthy. Do not write to unselected objects.\"}"
